## Data context

::: {.callout-note icon=false title="Structural equation models (SEM) in a nutshell"}
Analyse multivariate data $\mathbf y=(y_1,\dots,y_p)^\top$ to [**measure**]{.text-org} and [**relate**]{.text-grnn} *hidden* variables $\boldsymbol\eta=(\eta_1,\dots,\eta_q)^\top$, $q \ll p$, and uncover complex patterns.
:::

. . .

::: {.nudge-up-small}
In the social sciences, latent variables are used to represent **constructs**---the *theoretical, unobserved* concepts of interest.
:::

